  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Study visit on sustainable and value-based public procurement from Ukraine to the Netherlands</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project supports the logistics to implement a four full-days study visit on value-based procurement (VBP) and Sustainable Private Procurement (SPP) practices in the Netherlands. As result, eight representatives of two Ukrainian government bodies (MPU and MOH), working on the improvement of procurement processes and policies will be part of this visit. The members of the delegation will get practical understanding of the European standards for public procurement in the health sector through the knowledge, best practices and lessons learned of the Netherlands. The aim of this visit is to support the public healthcare sector in Ukraine through showcasing how Dutch health public buyers integrate value-based criteria into procurement; and on how Sustainable Private Procurement (SPP) policies and tools that incorporate environmental and social impacts alongside price are incorporated.  The project has a positive impact on the following Sustainable Development Goals (SDGs):SDG 8: Promote sustained, inclusive, and sustainable economic growth by strengthening procurement governance and opening opportunities for small- and medium--sized enterprises (SMEs);SDG 3: Ensure healthy lives and promote well-being by improving the quality and reliability of procured medical goods;SDG 12: Ensure sustainable consumption and production patterns through introduction of sustainability-oriented procurement criteria.</narrative>
  </description>
